  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "audio_sample_entry_box_read",
    "file": "gpac/src/isomedia/box_code_base.c",
    "description": "In the malformed-child fallback at line 4053, the function frees `ptr->esd` using `gf_isom_box_del_parent(&ptr->child_boxes, ...)`. For a QuickTime `wave`-nested ESDS, `audio_sample_entry_on_child_box` sets `ptr->esd` to the inner box but leaves ownership in the `wave` box's `child_boxes`. Removal from the MP4A entry's list therefore does nothing, yet the ESDS is freed. The `wave` child list retains the dangling pointer, which is dereferenced/freed again during movie teardown in `gf_isom_box_del`, causing the heap-use-after-free.",
    "conditions": "A parsed MP4A audio sample entry must contain a QuickTime `wave` child with an ESDS child, so `ptr->esd` aliases an object owned by `wave->child_boxes`. Subsequent malformed/truncated box or descriptor data must make the initial `gf_isom_box_array_read` fail and enter the raw-data ESDS recovery loop. When that scan finds an `esds` signature, line 4053 frees the existing nested ESDS through the wrong parent list; later recursive deletion of MP4A -> wave -> child_boxes accesses the freed box."
  },
